I agree.

All objects should have a WISHABLE flags, and most things should not be
wishable.  

There is no point making it dependant on your level - high-level characters
are already powerful enough (hehe... unless you make it inversely powerful
with level).

No artifact wishing.

Wishes only from Djinies, and make magic lamps indistinguishable from
oil lamps, except that they never run out.  (ie. calling oil-lamps
"foobar" would also label magic lamps as "foobar").  Reasoning?  It
isn't the LAMP that is magic, it's the CONTENTS.


As Mr Magnetic suggests, wishing places limits on how hard a player
will try to get something.  For example, why bother sacrificing for
Mjollnir when you might be able to WISH for a +2 Mjollnir.

